{
  "name": "OpenCloud \u2014 End-to-end smoke test",
  "meta": {
    "description": "**Opt-in live integration test.** Exercises every OpenCloud node operation against a real OpenCloud server. The repo test suite uses mocked HTTP via nock and runs in CI; this workflow is for manual end-to-end verification.\n\nBefore running:\n  1. Create an OpenCloud credential in n8n (Settings \u2192 Credentials). For local Docker dev, the typical URL is https://host.docker.internal:9200.\n  2. Patch this workflow with your credential id:\n       ./examples/apply-credentials.sh <credential-id> > /tmp/smoke.json\n     and import /tmp/smoke.json. Or import as-is and pick the credential on every node manually.\n\nNo drive id needed \u2014 the Resolve-space step calls /graph/v1.0/me/drives via the Space:List operation and the Config Code node picks the personal drive automatically. Works against any backend.\n\nWhat it does (in order):\n  0. Cleanup any pre-existing /n8n-smoke from a prior run (idempotent re-runs)\n  1. Create /n8n-smoke folder\n  2. Generate test bytes\n  3. Upload as /n8n-smoke/hello.txt\n  4. List /n8n-smoke\n  5. Download /n8n-smoke/hello.txt\n  6. Create /n8n-smoke/archive subfolder\n  7. Copy hello.txt \u2192 archive/copy.txt\n  8. Move archive/copy.txt \u2192 archive/renamed.txt\n  8a. Copy the archive folder → /n8n-smoke/archive-copy\n  8b. Move (rename) archive-copy → /n8n-smoke/archive-moved\n  8c. Create a public share link for the /n8n-smoke/archive folder\n  9. Create a public share link for hello.txt\n 10. Delete hello.txt\n 11. Delete /n8n-smoke (cleanup)\n\nA parallel branch exercises user management: create → get → rename → get-many → delete.\n\nA third branch covers project spaces: it provisions a project space (via the HTTP Request node — the OpenCloud node has no space:create), then runs folder:create, file:upload, file:copy and public-link shares (file + space) against it. It also creates a throwaway recipient user and exercises the invite path — file, folder and space shared TO a user (recipientType=user) — then deletes that user, and finally disables + purges the space. space:share needs a project space — a personal drive root rejects it with \"unsupported space type\" — which is why it lives here and not in the personal-drive branch. It also creates a throwaway group (again via the HTTP Request node — no group:create on the node) and shares the folder and space TO that group, then deletes the group.\n\nEach OpenCloud node has continueOnFail=true so one failing step does not abort the rest; the final Verify step aggregates per-step results and THROWS when any non-ignored step failed, so the execution (and the e2e assertion) fails loudly on a regression."
  },
